.TH smi-neo4j-query "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-neo4j-query \- Run Cypher against an embedded Neo4j database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-neo4j-query
.RB [ \-H
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR NAME = VALUE ]...
.RI [ CYPHER ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-neo4j-query
opens the embedded Neo4j database made by
.BR smi-neo4j-create-db (1)
and runs Cypher: the statement given as arguments, or, without one, the statements read from
standard input, each ended with
.B ;
at the end of a line. Each statement runs in a transaction of its own and is printed with its
result, a table of the returned rows or the counts of what it created, set or deleted. Lines
starting with
.B //
are comments.
.PP
The first statement that fails ends the command with exit status 1; the statements before it
stay committed.
.PP
A directory that is not a Neo4j database is an error, so a wrong path never creates a new one.
The database is embedded, so it can not be queried while another process has it open.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-home " " \fIDIR\fR
The database directory, default
.BR SMI_NEO4J_HOME .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-param " " \fINAME\fR=\fIVALUE\fR
A parameter, used as
.BI $ NAME
in the Cypher, as a string. Repeat for more.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_NEO4J_HOME
The database directory, as printed by
.BR smi-neo4j-create-db .
.TP
.B JAVA_OPTS
Further Java options, kept after the ones the command sets.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every statement ran.
.TP
.B 1
No database, no statement, or a failed statement, with the error of Neo4j on standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Populate from a file and query:
.RS
.nf
\&. ./graph.env
smi-neo4j-query < populate.cypher
smi-neo4j-query "MATCH (p:Person)-[:WORKS_AT]->(c:Company) RETURN p.name, c.name"
.fi
.RE
.PP
With a parameter, quoted for the shell so that
.B $name
reaches Cypher:
.RS
.nf
smi-neo4j-query -p name=Alice 'MATCH (:Person {name: $name})-[:KNOWS*]->(f) RETURN f.name'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Another database than the one of the environment:
.RS
.nf
smi-neo4j-query -H /srv/graphs/sales "MATCH (n) RETURN count(n)"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-neo4j-create-db (1),
.BR smi-query-db (1)
.SH AUTHOR
setmy.info
